{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #690: declared status 'solved'. Formalized: no. Let $d_k(p)$ be the density of those integers whose $k$th smallest prime factor is $p$ (i.e. if $p_1<p_2<\\cdots$ are the primes dividing $n$ then $p_k=p$).\n\nFor fixed $k\\geq 1$ is $d_k(p)$ unimodular in $p$? That is, it first increases in $p$ until its maximum then decreases. Current best: Cambie \\cite{Ca25} has shown that $d_k(p)$ is unimodular for $1\\leq k\\leq 3$ and is not unimodular for $4\\leq k\\leq 20$. Prize: no. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_befb0fd27f08cbda1fdacb6096f41d851182d2cf4df18bf8df3dc8254073f208","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:690","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_1ef7e98a41ecd48c","object_root":"sha256:cea7bdaa98e810950f509a22592c0110ef015fe82e56b1a2b96c26eb587f6f15","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:690"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}